# Welcome (first-run wizard), both looks.
setup foot &
wait 1
rec open 1.5 ipc welcome open
note Backdrop and card fade in over ~300 ms, card rises 12 px; NO drop shadow under the card (FAIL if a dark halo is visible below it).
wait 1
shot step1
note Step 1 of the welcome card, same layout as QML.
rec step2 1 key -k Return
note Enter moves to step 2: the new page slides in from the right (24 px, 250 ms) and fades (200 ms). Check the slide in the recording.
wait 0.6
key -k Escape
wait 0.6
shot back
note Esc goes back one step; the previous step slides in from the LEFT.
# Step 3: Dark
# MANUAL: Tab to "Dark" and press Space: the desktop behind switches to dark at once (config.json appearance.mode "dark")
# Step 4: wallpapers
# MANUAL: step 3 of the wizard: click "Dusk": ring moves to it and the wallpaper changes behind; hover another tile: faint ring (0.35); "Choose a picture..." opens the file picker (close it) (click on layer surfaces may not register in the harness)
# Step 5: finish
# MANUAL: last step: "Start using Tessera" fades out (~200 ms) and welcome.done is true; if the look changed, switch-look runs
# Step 6: later
# MANUAL: reopen, "Set up later" closes it, done = true
key -k Escape
wait 1
shot closed
note Welcome is closed or at its first step after Esc; compare with QML (Esc at step 1).
# Step 7: reduce motion
# MANUAL: appearance.reduceMotion true: open appears at once, steps change without sliding
